{# The assembled system prompt.

   TENANT-INVARIANT BY CONSTRUCTION. Nothing *here* interpolates a tenant, a traveller,
   a timestamp or a policy value — because everything in this file sits BEFORE the cache
   breakpoint, and anything varying before a breakpoint means no two requests share a
   cache entry. A tenant-specific value here would give every customer a private prefix:
   the exact opposite of the cost lesson this sample teaches.

   That is a rule about *placement*, not about variables. Per-session context — who the
   traveller is, what today's date is — is legitimate and lives after the breakpoint or in
   the message; see `prompts/manager.py:system_blocks`. Measured: three travellers across
   two tenants each read the same 1042 cached tokens.

   Ordering is most-stable-first so a cache point captures the largest possible prefix.
#}
